@startuml
top to bottom direction
skinparam backgroundColor #FCFCFD
skinparam defaultFontName SansSerif
skinparam defaultFontSize 18
skinparam defaultFontColor #172B4D
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundCorner 16
skinparam nodesep 35
skinparam ranksep 50
skinparam ArrowColor #475569
skinparam ArrowThickness 2
skinparam rectangle {
  BorderThickness 2
  BackgroundColor #FFFFFF
  BorderColor #475569
}
title EVPN-for-OVN | ownership and module boundaries

rectangle "Project integration / orchestration" as Integrations #FFFBF2 {
  rectangle "EVPN Operator\nEvpnCore YAML lifecycle\nReadiness / finalization" as Operator #FFF4DB
  rectangle "EVPN CNI Adapter\nADD / CHECK / DEL\nAttachment translation" as CNI #FFF4DB
  rectangle "Node-Agent\nEndpoint services / Type-2 loops\nCNI authority / runtime verification" as Agent #FFF4DB
  rectangle "Neutron / standalone adapters\nPLANNED platform integration" as Future #FFF4DB
}
rectangle "EVPN Core (logical responsibilities)" as Core #F5F9FF {
  rectangle "EVPN Type-2 import / export\nRoute validation / reconcile\nGoBGP route adapter" as Routes #E8F1FF
  rectangle "Endpoint reconciliation\nIdentity-owned ports\nand OVS attachments" as Endpoints #E8F1FF
  rectangle "OVN integration\nNetlink or OVSDB state\nAlternative network paths" as Integration #E8F1FF
  rectangle "Ownership and recovery\nFences / journals / receipts\nAmbiguous outcomes BLOCKED" as Recovery #E8F1FF
}
rectangle "Reused third-party solutions" as Reused #F8FAFC {
  rectangle "Kubernetes / containerd\nWorkloads / sandbox evidence" as Kube #F1F5F9
  rectangle "Multus\nExternal Kubernetes integration\nInvokes EVPN CNI Adapter" as Multus #F1F5F9
  rectangle "k8gobgp | independent\nBGPConfiguration owner\nManager + gobgpd image" as Provider #F1F5F9
  rectangle "GoBGP | reused BGP engine\nSessions, EVPN RIB, route gRPC" as GoBGP #F1F5F9
  rectangle "Linux / Netlink state\nIntegration FDB and neighbors" as Linux #F1F5F9
  rectangle "OVN / OVS\nNB / SB, northd, ovn-controller\nWorkload VXLAN forwarding" as OVN #F1F5F9
}
rectangle "External EVPN peers / VTEPs\nFRR / Linux acceptance peer" as Peers #F1F5F9

Operator --> Agent : deploys / configures
Kube --> Multus : CNI invocation
CNI --> Agent : Unix endpoint RPC
Future -[#925C00,dashed]-> Endpoints : target reuse
Agent --> Routes : runs Type-2 loops
Agent --> Endpoints : invokes services
Endpoints --> Integration : OVN / OVS attachment
Routes --> Integration : accepted route state
Integration -[hidden]right-> Recovery
Agent --> Kube : identity evidence
Operator --> Kube : workload reconciliation
Provider -[#475569]-> GoBGP : BGP identity / peers\nindependent writer
Routes <-[#2457A7]-> GoBGP : RIB reads / AddPath\nUUID-only DeletePath
Integration --> Linux : Netlink mode
Linux --> OVN : observed by ovn-controller
Integration --> OVN : alternative OVSDB mode
GoBGP <-[#2457A7]-> Peers : MP-BGP EVPN routes
OVN <-[#18724B]-> Peers : VXLAN packets

legend bottom
  |= Color / line |= Meaning |
  |<#E8F1FF> Blue | Project-owned core responsibilities |
  |<#FFF4DB> Amber | Project-owned optional integration / orchestration |
  |<#F1F5F9> Slate | Third-party implementations and infrastructure |
  | Solid / dashed + PLANNED | Implemented / design target |
  | Blue arrow / green arrow | Route control / packet forwarding |
endlegend
footer EVPN Core: logical core responsibilities - not a standalone runtime.\nRecovery spans core and runtime modules; platform independence remains a design target.
@enduml
